$\begin{align}
\text{vertex's }x\text{-coordinate}&=\dfrac{(\goldD{-2})+(\goldD{4})}{2}
\\\\
&=\blueD{1}
\end{align}$

Now we can find the vertex's $y$-coordinate by evaluating $f(\blueD{1})$:

$\begin{align}
f(\blueD{1})&=(\blueD{1}+2)(\blueD{1}-4)
\\\\
&=(3)(-3)
\\\\
&=-9
\end{align}$
